 2. ⛽️ No relief for energy prices 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: FactSet. Chart: Axios Markets/Matt Phillips Markets are coming around to the view that energy prices will stay high well into next year, Axios' Matt Phillips reports. 

 Brent crude futures contracts for April 2027 jumped to more than $85 a barrel this week. That's the highest since the war in Iran began in February, and higher than at the peak for oil prices back in early May. 💥 The upswing comes after drone attacks on an alternative crude oil export route to the Red Sea and on a key pipeline.

 The latest prices for Brent oil futures set for delivery over the next six months or so have jumped higher recently. (That's the pink line in the chart above, compared with the same contract prices a week, a month and a year ago.) Go deeper . 

 
 
